[CA]
Resolution approving Outside User Water/Sewer Services, by User’s Agreement, with Three
Rivers West, LLC, Lots 1-3, Block 2, Swan Ranch Rail Park, Third Filing, Laramie County, Wyoming
-- referred to Finance Committee (sponsors - Mr. Brown and Mr. Valdez).
[CA]
Resolution approving the Annual Budget for Fiscal Year 2011-2012 of the Laramie County
Community Juvenile Services Joint Powers Board -- referred to Finance Committee (sponsor - Mr.
Valdez).
[CA]
Resolution authorizing the Mayor to sign a Memorandum of Understanding with Laramie
County to apply for the Edward Byrne Memorial Justice Assistance Grant Program -- referred to
Finance Committee (sponsor - Mr. Brown).
[CA]
Resolution authorizing submission of an application to the Wyoming Business Council,
Business Ready Community Grant and Loan Program, for funding through the Downtown Development
Grant Program to provide a utility corridor to encourage development of downtown business space --
referred to Finance Committee (sponsors - Mr. Brown and Dr. Rinne).

Preliminary PUD Planned Unit Development (Zone Change) from MR-1 Medium Density
Residential-Established and P Public Districts for Blocks 138, 139, 172, 173 and 200, Original City,
Cheyenne, Wyoming (located between E. 22nd and E. 25th Streets, east of Warren and west of Evans
Avenues).  Bill Green, Christine Kronz, Scott Brugger, Janice Floth and Sunny Kaste spoke in favor
of the proposed PUD zone.  Comments included support for a comprehensive cancer facility with
parking availability at one location adjacent to the hospital, and economic benefits due to the hospital’s
proposed project.  David Squires, Senior Vice-President, Cheyenne Regional Medical Center, noted that
project plans will involve expansion of services, remodeling of certain areas, new building addition, and
a parking structure, and briefly reviewed major areas that will be included in the project.  Mr. Collins
moved to acknowledge receipt, seconded by Ms. Broyles.  Comment followed regarding the hospital’s
downtown location adjacent to a residential area, and suggestion that elements involving building
heights, architectural and design plans, green space, and parking structure height, as worded in the PUD
information affiliated with the agenda item, be clarified prior to the zone change ordinance being
introduced on the agenda.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present.
[CA]
Land Lease Agreement and Memorandum of Land Lease Agreement between the City of
Cheyenne and Verizon Wireless for installation and maintenance of a cell tower in North Cheyenne
Community Park.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.  (#5713)
[CA]
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Stride Learning Center to provide cooperative
transit services.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.  (#5714)
